    "summary": "Added scopeErrorMapping beside the three scope error classes: the one mapping from each class to its code, with the scope path and the registered repo for scope-not-indexed. The plan tree's and the daemon's mapping functions call it and return what they returned before. The plan walk calls it too, so a runtime that throws one of the three classes is recorded as failed with that code and the error's own message, with no 'runtime-threw:' prefix; any other error keeps the prefix and has no code. The task record and the entries of tasksFailed (the plan's, the run's, the run record's and the daemon's response) carry the optional code. The walk imports nothing from the run driver.",
